## II. Conscious Deliberation / Global Workspace Broadcasting

Dehaene, S., & Changeux, J. P. (2011). Experimental and Theoretical Approaches to Conscious
Processing. *Neuron*, 70(2), 200–227.
DOI: 10.1016/j.neuron.2011.03.018

**Claim supported:** The conscious layer's function — parallel processing streams converging
into a unified deliberative output broadcast widely before commitment — is consistent with
the Global Neuronal Workspace hypothesis as formalized by Dehaene & Changeux. Conscious
access correlates with coordinated broadcast across distributed networks, not with localized
processing. The architecture's multi-stream convergence before output commitment instantiates
this principle computationally.

